Obsidian Portal that have become deal breakers for me.<br /> <br /> First is the fact that development of Obsidian Portal has stagnated. I swear Obsidian Portal hasn't been updated with new and useful features in roughly a decade, something I'd think they'd do considering their their pricing plans.<br /> <br /> I also absolutely don't like the way OP's character page is displayed. My games tend to run NPC heavy, and after even a short while I find myself having to scroll a lot to find a specific NPC in the list. Even the ability to change the way the page displays to be a more compact view so more characters display in a smaller space would be appreciated. It's much easier to go through the character list (or any list) on Kanka than it is on Obsidian Portal.<br /> <br /> Lastly is that when doing a search on Obsidian Portal filtered for multiple tags, it includes everyone that had any of the tags selected instead of displaying only the characters with all the selected tags. Kanka's filters are really good, and you can even create custom menu links that display preset filters you've set up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T13:38:17-08:00","id":1369636,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I just emigrated my whole Chicago Requiem game to 